  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR158821 - Harmful alcohol use in Southern Africa: Studying  drivers of drinking to inform effective intervention (CHASE SA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The study aims to examine the context of the global alcohol environment and its influence on local alcohol environments, with a particular focus on alcohol environments in sub-Saharan Africa, specifically Botswana and South Africa. It addresses 4 research questions via 4 work packages (WPs) and each WP includes two to three sub-studies: 
Work package 1: Political, commercial, environmental, socio-cultural influences on harmful alcohol use alcohol in Southern Africa (South Africa and Botswana). 
Work package 2: Alcohol acquisition and consumption environments in Southern Africa (South Africa and Botswana).
Work package 3: Impacts of political, acquisition and consumption environment on alcohol in South Africa only. 
Work package 4: Harnessing community and policy maker voices to influence alcohol policy.</narrative>
  </description>
